.TH SDL_DestroyAudioStream 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_DestroyAudioStream \- Free an audio stream.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_audio.h>
.PP
.BI "void SDL_DestroyAudioStream(SDL_AudioStream *stream);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This will release all allocated data, including any audio that is still queued\[char46] You do not need to manually clear the stream first\[char46]
.PP
If this stream was bound to an audio device, it is unbound during this call\[char46] If this stream was created with
.BR SDL_OpenAudioDeviceStream ,
the audio device that was opened alongside this stream\(aqs creation will be closed, too\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I stream
the audio stream to destroy\[char46]
.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_CreateAudioStream (3)
